            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Power",
               "Pi",
               2
            ],
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral \\( \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 2 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\) needs integration by parts once more, with the polynomial factor as the new u; it equals \\( 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4} - \\left(2\\right) = -2 + \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{4} \\).",
